{
 "artist": {
  "bio": "Statement\n\nMy name is Karen Ebbs and I am Dublin-born visual artist with years of professional practice, working from my studio at the Digital Hub, Dublin. I am an alumna of NCAD and the RHA School. I hold first class honours degrees for both an MA and a BA in Fine Art in Painting from NCAD. Following my MA I was shortlisted for the RDS visual Artis Awards, 2023. I am a member of Pallas Projects + Studios.\n\nAbstract painting and colour are central to my practice and visual language. I paint to interpret the world around me and explore the mystery of existence. Painting is my way of thinking and processing my experience of reality. I work across painting, sculpture and installation, using oil paint, porcelain, aluminium, plexiglass and wood. I create large-scale, luminous colour fields through gestural mark-making and recurring motifs. Elements are often installed as immersive spaces enveloping the viewer.\n\nRooted in a fascination with perception and how it occurs, my work begins with the belief that seeing is never passive; what we perceive is inseparable from who we are. I have an intuitive relationship with colour which is underpinned by research in colour theory, perceptual psychology, philosophy and neuroscience.\n\nBio Selection\n\nI have exhibited widely in group shows including the RHA annual, Boyle Arts Festival, and Draoicht Arts Centre. Recent solo exhibitions include ‘An Outer Reflection of an Inner Reality’, Municipal Gallery, dlr Lexicon (2025) (open call solo award), ‘Circumambulation’, Rathfarnham Castle OPW (2024), ‘Wild Accumulations’, The LAB Gallery (2022), and ‘I Am More Blue Than You’, Farmleigh Estate OPW. I received the Arts Council Agility Award (2022) and Dún Laoghaire Professional Development Award (2022).",
  "county": null,
  "display_name": "Karen Ebbs",
